n cling to a life like a  coward without honor in this case  momonosuke  saying his real name is his ultimate  redemption the ultimate courageous act  which  fully pays respect to his parents who  sacrificed their lives to save him  denying his name would be like denying  his  parents and denying his duty and momo  refuses to do that no matter what  just like momo drew inspiration from  luffy and shows bravery and honor  we can draw inspiration from this little  kid who showed courage  in the face of the strongest creature in  the world people are shocked and laugh  but kaido was clearly bothered he didn't  want to kill the kid and perhaps it also  irritates him  how much momo is like odin and how  despite  all of his power he cannot break the  little kid's spirit  after this moment of redemption momo  says he can finally face his parents in  the afterlife proudly  yes he does cry but he can't really help  that what he could do was decide his  path  and he chose the manliest one possible  so those are  manly tears dammit huge props to  momonosuke  he made us all very proud we then see an  explosion and luffy and yamato are  behind it  yamato is furious that her father was  willing to actually kill her and she  says that she gets it now  and that kaido is no longer her father  she's crying clearly emotional  but who can blame her this is about as  bad as daddy issues go this was a  significant realization though  because it should have cut yamato's ties  to her dad  so she can fully focus on the fight and  not hesitate as a result of sympathy  or unresolved feelings it turns out  luffy made it in time and he says that  and i quote  the decisive battle is about to start  end quote  remove all hype limiters that is what we  needed to hear  and now all systems are go the red  scabbards sneak up behind kaido  everyone is shocked especially queen in  his stereotypical over-the-top fashion  jack is shocked to see the mink rulers  alive and will hopefully get to see them  w